From: juniorverli <25966843+juniorverli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: edp: Add LG Display LP129WT342166

The LCD Surface Pro 11 reports LGD product 0x077b and places its
2880x1920 timings in a DisplayID 2.0 extension. Add its identity to the
EDID panel table.

Use the existing conservative LGD delay profile, also used by the
LP129WT232166 family member. These are provisional family defaults,
not measured timings for LP129WT342166; the Windows panel timing
requirements have not yet been established. Mode timings remain
provided by EDID.

Assisted-by: Codex gpt-6.1-sol
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-edp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-edp.c
index 2b455369e..09c052f58 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-edp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-edp.c
@@ -2187,6 +2187,7 @@ static const struct edp_panel_entry edp_panels[] = {
 	EDP_PANEL_ENTRY('L', 'G', 'D', 0x05f1, &delay_200_500_e200_d200, "Unknown"),
 	EDP_PANEL_ENTRY('L', 'G', 'D', 0x06b2, &delay_200_500_e200_d200, "LP129WT232166"),
 	EDP_PANEL_ENTRY('L', 'G', 'D', 0x0778, &delay_200_500_e200_d200, "134WT1"),
+	EDP_PANEL_ENTRY('L', 'G', 'D', 0x077b, &delay_200_500_e200_d200, "LP129WT342166"),
 	EDP_PANEL_ENTRY('L', 'G', 'D', 0x07fe, &delay_200_500_e200_d200, "LP116WHA-SPB1"),
 
 	EDP_PANEL_ENTRY('S', 'H', 'P', 0x1511, &delay_200_500_e50, "LQ140M1JW48"),
